---
arrangement: why-nothing-to-report
when-used: The whole zero-argument `dorc why` render when no trust was spent, nothing diverged, and nothing is improvable. Value: the book name.
why: The quiet case still answers the question asked, rather than printing an empty set of section headings.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- why-nothing-to-report && mise run loom:promote -- why-nothing-to-report`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all why-nothing-to-report` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# Only no-target-state builtins: nothing to probe, nothing to describe, nothing to say.
cd /var/tmp
true

-- replay --
$ dorc why --book=book.sh
